  "comments": "<p>The tuatara is a native lizard to New Zealand and one of the oldest of all living reptiles. It grows up to 0.6m in length and can be traced back 180 million years. The tuatara has been given special protection by an Act of Parliament.<br><br><i>Obverse die varieties:</i><br><strong>KM#34.1</strong> <i>(1967-85)</i> Rounded high relief portrait;<br><strong>KM#34.2</strong> <i>(1985 only)</i> Die recut, low relief portrait;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>To see varieties between the circulation and BU/Proof coins please see here:</p><p><a class=\"n-link\" data-mention=\"N#1846\" data-n-number=\"1846\" data-issuer=\"New Zealand\" title=\"1 Cent - Elizabeth II (2nd portrait)\" href=\"/1846\">N#1846</a><br><br><i>1980 date varieties:</i><br><strong>Business strike for circulation</strong> ovoid 0 in date;<br><strong>BU &amp; Proof strike for set issue</strong> round O in date;<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5e4d3a6baeb44.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5e4d3a6baeb44.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br><i>1982 date varieties:</i><br>Blunt 2 in date:<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5bf72708a383c.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5bf72708a383c.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br>Pointed 2 in date (in sets):<br><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5bf7275c1c085.jpg\" alt=\"\"><br><br><i>Reverse die varieties:</i><br><strong>Die A</strong> <i>(1967-81 all issues, 1983-84 MS/PS, 1985 PS)</i> 5 weak waves at left side, the triangle of tail under the chin consists of separate scales.<br><strong>Die B</strong> <i>(1982)</i> similar to A, the scales in the triangle reengraved. It is easy to distinguish it by an additional scale at the top of the triangle.<br><strong>Die C</strong> <i>(1985)</i> 7 enhanced waves, the triangle of tail under the chin consists of separate scales.<br><strong>Die D</strong> - 5 enhanced waves, the triangle of tail under the chin consists of undivided scales.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/613db1dce2dad.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/613db1dce2dad.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br><i>Abbreviations:</i> MS - mint set, PS - proof set.<br><br><i>1967:</i><br><strong>with</strong> sea line right of Tuatara, common:<br><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5a2d6d5b7cc5d.jpg\" alt=\"\"><br><strong>without</strong> sea line right of Tuatara, rare:<br><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5a2d6d793ec53.jpg\" alt=\"\"><br><br>Reports have been received regarding a 1967 dated piece where the tail triangle under the chin appears to be missing from the reverse. This is not a recognised variety and may be the result of a worn die.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/623557d53dc51.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/623557d53dc51.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br>These coins were demonetized and withdrawn from circulation in 2006 and many will have been melted down.</p>",
